WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.590
(pensive music)

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:02.820
- [Narrator] Moscow said it captured

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:04.710
the Eastern Ukrainian town of Soledar,

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:07.183
which would be its first
major gain since July.

00:00:07.183 --> 00:00:08.310
(gun firing)

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:10.560
Kiev says the fighting
around the town continues

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:13.287
but Russian state media
is already celebrating.

00:00:13.287 --> 00:00:14.898
(reporter 1 speaking in foreign language)

00:00:14.898 --> 00:00:16.740
(reporter 2 speaking in foreign language)

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:19.230
The reports have amplified
the strategic importance

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:20.460
of this small town

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.080
as Russia's recent advances there

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.640
offer President Vladimir Putin

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.710
a rare opportunity to celebrate.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.420
- It's allowed him to claim a victory

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:30.043
after a series of very humiliating losses.

00:00:30.043 --> 00:00:31.890
(gun firing)
(dramatic music)

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:33.030
- [Narrator] But the reality on the ground

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:35.790
is more complicated than
propaganda reports suggests,

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:38.590
highlighting the questions
about what's next in the war.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.090
Soledar, a town with a pre-war population

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:44.430
of 10,000 people has been the focal point

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:47.493
of Russia's offensive and
media coverage in recent weeks.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:51.390
It is just a few miles north
of the larger city of Bakhmut,

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:53.160
which Russia has unsuccessfully tried

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:54.633
to seize for months now.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:57.564
Russian media has described both Soledar

00:00:57.564 --> 00:01:00.083
and Bakhmut as critical for Ukraine.

00:01:00.083 --> 00:01:05.083
(reporter 3 speaking in foreign language)

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:08.460
But Western officials and
military analysts are skeptical

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:10.170
about Soledar's importance.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.457
- Get what's been
happening over the last 10

00:01:11.457 --> 00:01:12.290
and a half months,

00:01:12.290 --> 00:01:13.380
particularly in the Donbas.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:16.893
Towns and villages have
swapped hands quite frequently.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:18.840
- [Narrator] And beyond Soledar,

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:21.780
even if Bakhmut fails,
defense experts say the cost

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:24.210
of six months of fighting
in the area far outweighs

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:26.400
any operational advantage for Moscow.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:30.090
- It has been the most
brutal theater in the war

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:34.410
over the last six months, and
Western intelligence estimates

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:37.230
that each side in the conflict has now had

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:39.240
about 100,000 casualties.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:40.980
- [Narrator] Recent
satellite images also show

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:42.090
numerous bomb craters

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:43.740
from artillery all over Bakhmut,

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:45.780
suggesting Russia has spent high volumes

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:48.060
of ammunition in the offensive.

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:50.970
The price Russia pays for the
contested territory is missing

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:52.590
from the state media coverage

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:54.540
while reports highlight the heavy losses

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:56.232
suffered by Ukraine.

00:01:56.232 --> 00:01:59.400
(reporter 4 speaking in foreign language)

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:02.220
- We don't have exact
estimates for Ukrainian losses

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:04.200
but Ukrainian officials
have repeatedly said

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.030
that the fighting is is very difficult

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:08.280
and there have been heavy
losses on both sides.

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:10.050
- [Narrator] Now, even
if the state propaganda

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:13.447
is enthusiastic about the
prospects of Russia's campaign,

00:02:13.447 --> 00:02:16.800
(reporter 5 speaking in foreign language)

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.020
Ukraine says the celebration is premature

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:20.416
as fighting continues.

00:02:20.416 --> 00:02:21.420
(bombs exploding)

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:24.090
- The big question is
if Ukraine can regroup

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:26.070
and establish a second line

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:29.160
of defense and stop Russian
advances where they are

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:31.367
or if Russians will
continue to break through,

00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:34.020
and if it's the first scenario,

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.060
then this will not be
a very significant loss

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.860
for Ukrainians.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:41.459
And if it's the second, it
could have a larger impact.

00:02:41.459 --> 00:02:44.126
(pensive music)

